{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"2269109bc7123a3e","name":"card_event_hms_spectre","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/NavalWarfare/events/card_event_hms_spectre","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"HMS SCEPTRE","text":"Counter an enemy order then Convert it to PLAN and return it to hand.","flavorText":"HMS Sceptre was an S-class submarine of the Royal Navy commissioned in 1943. It was built by Scotts Shipbuilding and Engineering Company, and deployed primarily in the North Sea and Norwegian waters. Sceptre conducted patrols and offensive operations against German naval and merchant vessels, including laying mines and launching torpedo attacks. Sceptre played a role in Operation Source in 1943, supporting attacks against German battleships in Norwegian fjords, though she did not participate directly in the X-craft midget submarine attacks. Another of her notable missions involved the sinking of a couple German merchant ships and damaging others during convoy attacks in the Bay of Biscay in May 1944. Throughout her service in WWII, HMS Sceptre completed multiple patrols and contributed to the disruption of Axis maritime activity in northern European waters. She remained in service until the end of the war and was eventually scrapped in 1949.","faction":"Britain","type":"gotcha","rarity":"Common","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"GameplayTags":["subtype.navy"],"Name":"card_event_hms_spectre","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_hms_spectre_title","SourceString":"HMS SCEPTRE","LocalizedString":"HMS SCEPTRE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::gotcha","faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_hms_spectre_text","SourceString":"Counter an enemy order then Convert it to PLAN and return it to hand.","LocalizedString":"Counter an enemy order then Convert it to PLAN and return it to hand."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Ke